div.p:
Captain T. J. Page, from Virginia; R. R. Carter, first lieutenant, from Virginia;
                    Geo. S. Shryock, second lieutenant, from Kentucky; Geo. T. Bochart, third
                    lieutenant, from Savannah, Ga.; E. G. Reed, third lieutenant, from Virginia;
                    Samuel Barron, jr., third lieutenant, from Virginia; E. Green, surgeon, from
                    Virginia; C. W. Curtis, paymaster, from South Carolina; W. P. Brooks, chief
                    engineer, from South Carolina; J. W. Herty, assistant surgeon, from Georgia; W.
                    W. Wilkenson, master, from South Carolina; W. Hutcheson Jackson, first assistant
                    engineer, from Baltimore; J. C. Cosh, second assistant engineer, from Texas;
                    John W. Dukeheart, boatswain, from Baltimore; J. W. King, gunner, from North
                    Carolina; J. Mather, carpenter, from Maryland; William Savage, master’s mate,
                    from Maryland; William Baynton, paymaster’s clerk, from Florida John W. Prior,
                    sergeant of marines, from Virginia.
